Okay, great! `Rails.error` is definitely configured, confirmed in `config/initializers/error_context.rb`.  Now, it's time to dive into **Area 5**: the Notification Settings UI and its accompanying Stimulus controller (`notifications_controller.js`). This is where we make sure everything clicks!

I need to meticulously examine *every single detail* of those templates and stylesheets: `notifications.css`, `_browser.html.erb`, `_install.html.erb`, `_system.html.erb`, `show.html.erb`, `_email.html.erb`, and `_head.html.erb`. The HTML structure and the Stimulus controller must perfectly align with Design's CSS and all the partials. I'm talking 100% precision here!

